---
// The standing "this was written with AI" note. Rendered on any post with
// `aiAssisted: true` in its frontmatter, so the wording stays identical
// everywhere and changes in one place. It is deliberately not a changelog:
// per-post revisions belong in the post.
//
// An <aside> with a label, not a <section> with an <h2>: it's a note about the post, not
// part of its content, so it stays out of the heading outline and reads as a callout.
---

<aside class="post-provenance" aria-labelledby="post-provenance-label">
  <p class="post-provenance__label" id="post-provenance-label">How this post was written</p>
  <p>
    I didn't write the prose. Claude did, working from transcripts of the sessions where the
    work happened. I chose the subject, made the decisions it describes, and edited.
  </p>
  <p>Every source is linked, so check anything that matters to you. Errors are mine.</p>
</aside>
